	(text_box "Each channel, left to right: SMA (50 Ω or high-Z by jumper)\n-> 100 Ω and a diode clamp to the rails\n-> source jumper: the SMA, or NOISE (channel A) / ALT (channel B: NOISE or the photodiode)\n-> two OPA1612 stages, each x1 or x10 by jumper -> U.FL monitor tap\n-> THS4521 fully differential driver, gain 1 -> 33 Ω + 22 pF -> AD9238.\n-3 dB at 23 MHz at x1 (sim/adc_frontend.cir). The details stand beside each block.\nBoth sample clocks come from the FPGA, so the gateware owns the phase."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 25.4 0)
		(size 93.98 16.51)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 194 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b4d34040-6b3b-fa82-ccc7-681841aca86b")
	)
	(text_box "Either channel can select it (its SRC / ALT jumper).\nA resistor at room temperature makes √(4kTR) of noise:\n1.3 nV/√Hz at 100 Ω, 12.9 nV/√Hz at 10 kΩ.\nSwitch one in (the DIP switch) or plug your own\ninto J105. With both channels on the same resistor,\nthe cross-spectrum averages away each amplifier's\nown noise and leaves the resistor's. Switch 0 Ω in\nto measure the amplifiers alone."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 306.07 0)
		(size 49.53 15.24)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 194 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.95 0.95)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b5a50f28-c8ac-8d1c-c4e6-7aacc0b4533b")
	)
	(text_box "Grounds: AGND and DRGND are one plane on this board.\nThe converter sits on the analog side of the floorplan with the FPGA's bus the only digital thing near it."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 400.05 317.5 0)
		(size 88.9 6.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 194 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.95 0.95)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "da59453e-3adc-2ab6-0961-7624c68ec1ce")
	)
	(text_box "VBPW34S PIN photodiode: 430-1100 nm, 60 % of its peak at\nthe red LED's 625 nm. Reverse biased 4.2 V into a\ntransimpedance amplifier, 10 kΩ: 10 mV per µA.\n2.2 pF across it: 6.8 MHz, 3.5 dB of peaking at 4 MHz\n(sim/tia.cir; 3.3 pF flattens it).\nAn external photodiode plugs into J106 (cathode to the\ntop pin). Light makes the output go positive.\nAim it at the LED on another board's DAC 1 for the\nlock-in-across-the-room experiment."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 149.86 306.07 0)
		(size 53.34 17.78)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 194 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.95 0.95)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e6b3d727-5f12-5253-a9d5-33f0dc9e3c81")
	)
